{
  "$comment": [
    "Permission profile for headless pipeline agents — the DEFAULT for every MODE.",
    "run_lane.sh launches each agent with `--permission-mode dontAsk --settings <this file>",
    "--output-format json` and logs every run (denials included) to $LOGDIR/denials.jsonl.",
    "LEM_PERMISSION_PROFILE=off is the emergency opt-out (docs/agent-pipeline-v2.md section 8).",
    "",
    "dontAsk = anything not allowed below is DENIED, never prompted (there is no human to ask).",
    "Settings MERGE across sources: user and project allow rules still apply, and a deny from ANY",
    "source wins. That is why several denies below repeat what the narrow allows already exclude.",
    "",
    "GUARD RAILS, NOT A BOUNDARY: a rule matches the command text an agent writes. Code an allowed",
    "command runs (pytest) executes as the runner's uid and can rewrite this file, the helper in",
    "lib/ and config.env. Root custody of those paths is the boundary (owner action).",
    "",
    "Narrow on purpose (docs/agent-pipeline-v2.md, 'Permission profile'):",
    "- git rebase: only the four forms MODE=rebase uses; git accepts abbreviated long options, so",
    "  no deny list can fence off --exec under a broad allow.",
    "- git push: denied in EVERY form; agents push via lib/git_push.sh, which pushes only the checked-out",
    "  run branch to itself (no refspec argument exists). A rule ending in `:*` is a trailing wildcard",
    "  to Claude Code, so 'deny any refspec colon' cannot be written as a pattern at all.",
    "- GitHub GraphQL only via lib/review_threads.sh; `gh api` stays denied.",
    "- File-reading flags git can abbreviate are denied by prefix (`--out*`, `--pathspec*`, `--no-in*`);",
    "  git add/rm/diff paths that are absolute, ~, $VAR or contain .. are denied. Helper body files are",
    "  realpath-checked, non-symlink, and copied before use.",
    "- Every gh WRITE (labels, assignees, issues, PRs, comments, draft toggles) only via lib/gh_safe.sh,",
    "  which sees the EXPANDED arguments, pins the repo, refuses to add the provenance-gated labels",
    "  and scopes writes to this run's issue/PR. Raw gh is read-only (view/diff/checks/list/run).",
    "- Commits only via lib/git_commit.sh (-m, or -F tmp/<name>); `git commit` is denied in every form.",
    "",
    "Keep `hooks` OUT of `permissions`: a hooks key nested inside the permission block voids the block.",
    "This profile defines no hooks; the user and project settings keep theirs."
  ],
